  "instance_name": "racial_violence_as_crime",
  "label": "The concept that racially motivated violence is a crime",
  "description": "Racially motivated violence is often considered a crime, as it violates laws and moral principles that protect human life and dignity. In the meme, the implication that killing zombies (non-human entities) is not homicide is used to downplay or justify racially motivated violence, thereby challenging the concept that racially motivated violence is a crime. This requires understanding of the concept of racial violence as a crime and its moral/legal implications.",
